0.9.40 — the word drift replaces the carbon rain in the loading pool: columns of plain English fall one letter to a printed square, strike the bottom rule, are thrown off it and settle into a heap along the floor — how deep the heap is, is how long you have waited. Sixteen things the office might say while you wait, from LOADING and STAND BY to DO NOT ADJUST YOUR SET and PATIENCE IS APPRECIATED. The rain's 78 writing systems and 5987 generated characters are retired; the wait is now said in words you can read
